{"version":2,"text":"Text C\n\nAN ALGORITHM FOR THE IDENTIFICATION AND MANAGEMENT OF ADULTS WITH IRON DEFICIENCY\n\nPatient presents with clinically suspected iron deficiency\n• member of high-risk population (infants, children, menstruating or pregnant\nwomen, vegetarians)\n• clinical or laboratory evidence of iron deficiency or anaemia\n• micocytosis or hypochromasia (MCV or MCH below laboratory lower limit of\nnormal)\n\n• Evaluate clinically for\n- potential contributors and risk factors for iron deficiency\n- inflammatory states or other disorders that may influence interpretation of FBC or iron studies\n• Measure serum ferritin level if not already measured\n\nSerum ferritin <30mcg/L\n\nIron deficiency\n\nEvaluate for cause (see\nBox 2)\n\nSerum ferritin 30-100 mcg/L\n\n• Borderline iron stores\n• Iron deficiency not excluded as serum\nferritin level may be raised because of\ninflammation\n\nIf iron deficiency felt\nto be contributory\n\n• Replace iron\n- give oral iron preparation\n- if rapid correction required (poorly tolerated anaemia)\nor oral therapy unsuccessful then give intravenous iron\n\nSerum ferritin >100 mcg/L\n\n• Iron deficiency unlikely\n• If anaemia present then consider\nfunctional iron deficiency; specialist input\nmay be required\n\nIf inflammatory state\nidentified\n\n• Correct inflammatory state\n• Selected patients may still\nbenefit from iron replacement;\nspecialist input advised\n\n• Re-evaluate 1 to 2 weeks after therapy to ensure iron stores are replete and anaemia improving\n• Re-evaluate 3 to 6 months after therapy to ensure iron repletion is maintained and anaemia resolved\n\nIf iron deficiency recurs\n• repeat evaluation for additional or recurrent source of blood loss;\nconsider all diagnoses in Box 2\n• refer men aged over 40 years and women over 50 years for\nendoscopy and colonoscopy regardless of gastrointestinal symptoms\n\nIf anaemia identified\nwith normal iron stores\n• evaluate for other\ncauses of anaemia\n\nPage 231","layout":{"version":1,"width":595.0,"height":842.0,"blocks":[{"text":"Text C","lines":[{"text":"Text C","x":0.12911206722689075,"y":0.16641439548693587,"width":0.07179912941176471,"height":0.018466318289786197,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Text","x":0.12911206722689075,"width":0.048338662184873954,"confidence":1},{"text":"C","x":0.1840200369747899,"width":0.01689115966386555,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"AN ALGORITHM FOR THE IDENTIFICATION AND MANAGEMENT OF ADULTS WITH IRON DEFICIENCY","lines":[{"text":"AN ALGORITHM FOR THE IDENTIFICATION AND MANAGEMENT OF ADULTS WITH IRON DEFICIENCY","x":0.24849293613445378,"y":0.20007203087885983,"width":0.5052748890756302,"height":0.009258591448931128,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"AN","x":0.24849293613445378,"width":0.015414554621848745,"confidence":1},{"text":"ALGORITHM","x":0.2666908302521009,"width":0.06340083025210082,"confidence":1},{"text":"FOR","x":0.332874931092437,"width":0.020970053781512604,"confidence":1},{"text":"THE","x":0.3563008050420168,"width":0.021115369747899175,"confidence":1},{"text":"IDENTIFICATION","x":0.38019278151260505,"width":0.08407461512605041,"confidence":1},{"text":"AND","x":0.4670507361344538,"width":0.022680297478991595,"confidence":1},{"text":"MANAGEMENT","x":0.4925143915966387,"width":0.07744159159663863,"confidence":1},{"text":"OF","x":0.5724071865546219,"width":0.013838447058823545,"confidence":1},{"text":"ADULTS","x":0.5890289714285715,"width":0.0407830588235294,"confidence":1},{"text":"WITH","x":0.6325953697478992,"width":0.027696978151260463,"confidence":1},{"text":"IRON","x":0.6630756857142858,"width":0.0259945630252101,"confidence":1},{"text":"DEFICIENCY","x":0.6918535865546218,"width":0.06191423865546221,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"Patient presents with clinically suspected iron deficiency\n• member of high-risk population (infants, children, menstruating or pregnant\nwomen, vegetarians)\n• clinical or laboratory evidence of iron deficiency or anaemia\n• micocytosis or hypochrom